This repository contains or modifies work from the projects below.

1. EMOVA speech tokenizer (UVITS unit-to-speech decoder and SPIRAL/FSQ
   speech-to-unit encoder)
   https://github.com/emova-ollm/EMOVA_speech_tokenizer
   Copyright the EMOVA authors. Licensed under the Apache License,
   Version 2.0; a copy is in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.
   Paper: "EMOVA: Empowering Language Models to See, Hear and Speak with
   Vivid Emotions", arXiv:2409.18042.

   examples/dynin-voice/dynin_vocoder.cpp and dynin_vocoder.h are a C++/ggml
   re-implementation of the UVITS decoder in that repository
   (speech_tokenization/UVITS/models.py, modules.py, attentions.py and
   transforms.py); where it helps trace a mismatch, the source comments
   name the Python module a section mirrors.
   tools/convert_emova_u2s_to_gguf.py follows the same
   code's tensor names, shapes and weight_norm layout. Changes: the Python /
   PyTorch modules were re-expressed in C++ and ggml, and the checkpoint is
   converted to GGUF. The EMOVA U2S weights themselves are not included in
   this repository; the separately published emova_u2s.gguf release asset
   is a format conversion of the Apache-2.0 checkpoint
   Emova-ollm/emova_speech_tokenizer_hf and remains under Apache-2.0.

   examples/dynin-voice/dynin_units.h and dynin_units.cpp are a C++/ggml
   re-implementation of the S2U (speech-to-unit) encoder in the same
   repository (speech_tokenization/SPIRAL_L2_BN_FSQ_CTC/: the SPIRAL model
   code and configuration, its hparams.yaml, and my_scripts/fsq.py).
   Changes: the PyTorch mel frontend, convolution and transformer stages
   and the FSQ quantizer were re-expressed in C++ and ggml, and the
   weights are read from a GGUF. The S2U weights and the script that
   converts them to GGUF are not included in this repository or its
   release.

   Upstream notices carried by that code, reproduced here as attribution:
   - SPIRAL (Huang et al., arXiv:2201.10207): source files marked
     "Copyright (C) 2021. Huawei Technologies Co., Ltd." and
     "Copyright (C) 2022. Huawei Technologies Co., Ltd.", Apache-2.0.
   - NVIDIA NeMo, on which the SPIRAL code is built: "Copyright (c) 2020,
     NVIDIA CORPORATION", Apache-2.0.
   - my_scripts/fsq.py: "Copyright 2023 Google LLC", Apache-2.0, modified
     from https://github.com/google-research/google-research/blob/master/fsq/fsq.ipynb
     (Finite Scalar Quantization, Mentzer et al., arXiv:2309.15505).

